WEEK 1 | Commit 7

CHANGES:
- Created TypeScript type definitions for authentication (AuthUser, AuthStatus, AuthMeResponse)
- Implemented AuthProvider React context with full user state management
- Added useAuth() hook for consuming auth state across the entire application

DETAILS:
- auth.ts types: AuthUser { id, email, preferred_lang, theme, created_at }
- auth.ts types: AuthStatus = 'loading' | 'authenticated' | 'unauthenticated'
- auth.ts types: AuthMeResponse { authenticated: boolean, user: AuthUser | null }
- AuthProvider: Fetches GET /api/auth/me on mount to restore session from httpOnly cookie
- AuthProvider: Manages status transitions: loading -> authenticated OR unauthenticated
- Exposes via useAuth(): user (AuthUser|null), status, refresh(), logout()
- refresh(): Re-fetches /api/auth/me to synchronize state after login or signup
- logout(): Calls POST /api/auth/logout to clear httpOnly cookie, then resets local state
- Error handling: Network failures gracefully fall back to 'unauthenticated' status
- Context prevents unnecessary re-renders by memoizing the provider value

FILES: src/types/auth.ts (new), src/lib/auth/auth-context.tsx (new)
